---
description: Conventions for the Express server
globs: ["server/**"]
alwaysApply: false
---

- ES modules (import/export), not CommonJS.
- Mongoose for MongoDB access; one model file per collection in server/models.
- One router file per resource in server/routes; keep controllers thin.
- All Razorpay SDK calls live in server/services/razorpay.js — nowhere else.
- Read RAZORPAY_KEY_ID / RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET from process.env, never hardcode.
- Every route that can fail (bad merchant id, Razorpay API error) returns a
  proper HTTP status and JSON error body, not a stack trace.